[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

; FOUNDATION alphabet block -- the approved hybrid block with a moulded wooden
; rim, so the cream letter face reads as INSET rather than applied.
;
; ⛔ THE LETTERS ARE NOT IN THE GLB AND NEVER WERE. `foundation_block.glb`
; ships five BLANK cream plaques named Front/Right/Back/Left/Top; every letter
; on every face is a runtime Label3D in THIS file, set by
; `alphabet_block.gd::update_letter()`. That is why the block had no letters
; until this scene existed -- there was no scene, not a missing texture.
;
; The geometry the labels depend on is unchanged from hybrid and is checked at
; BUILD time by `asset.verify_contract`: the plaque surface sits 0.413 from the
; block's centre and each label sits 0.4178, which is 0.0048 clear of it. The
; new rim rises to 0.427, so each letter now sits 0.009 DOWN INSIDE a shallow
; tray. It is still in front of its own plaque, which is what matters.
;
; font_size 83 and the 0.0847 label lift are carried over from hybrid
; UNCHANGED, deliberately -- see PROGRESS.md: both are believed wrong by a
; factor of 1.203, and that is a separate fix that needs its own browser check.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://alphabet_block/alphabet_block.gd" id="1"]
